s is significant as it can elevate uric acid levels, potentially impacting health and leading to related medical conditions.", "FEBUXOSTAT:El febuxostat es un inhibidor utilizado en el tratamiento de la hiperuricemia, que afecta la producción de ácido úrico.", "HIPOXANTINA:Hipoxantina is an enzyme that plays a crucial role in the degradation of purines within the human body. It facilitates the conversion of guanosine into guanine, thereby participating in the metabolic processes associated with purines. Additionally, hipoxantina serves as an intermediary in purine metabolism, where it is further converted into xantina. This highlights its importance in the biochemical pathways that manage purine levels in the body.", "GUANINA:Guanina, also known as guanine, is a purine base that plays a crucial role in the structure of nucleic acids in living organisms. It is produced from guanosine and is involved in various metabolic processes. In addition, guanina is metabolized through intermediates such as hypoxanthine and xanthine, ultimately leading to the formation of uric acid. This highlights its significance not only in genetic material but also in metabolic pathways within the body.", "XANTINA:Xantina is a compound that is formed during the metabolism of purines. It specifically arises from the degradation of purines, particularly through the breakdown of hypoxanthine and guanine. Ultimately, xantina is converted into uric acid, which is a key component in the purine metabolism pathway.", "CÁLCULOS DE ÁCIDO ÚRICO:Los cálculos de ácido úrico son depósitos sólidos que se forman en la orina debido a la baja solubilidad del ácido úrico.", "GUANOSINA:La guanosina es un nucleósido que se forma a partir de la degradación de las purinas y se convierte en guanina.", "ADENOSINA:La adenosina es un nucleósido que se forma a partir de la degradación de las purinas y se convierte en inosina.", "NUCLEÓSIDO:Los nucleósidos son compuestos formados por una base nitrogenada unida a un azúcar, que son productos intermedios en el metabolismo de las purinas.", "URATO:", "URICASA:Uricasa is an enzyme that converts uric acid into allantoin, which is more easily excreted from the body.", "GOTA:GOTA, also known as gout, is a form of inflammatory arthritis that arises from the body's inflammatory response to the deposition of monosodium urate crystals in joints and tissues, primarily due to elevated levels of uric acid. This condition is characterized by sudden and severe attacks of pain, swelling, and redness in the affected joints. GOTA is often associated with the formation of uric acid stones, which can occur as a result of the high uric acid levels in the body. Overall, GOTA represents a clinical syndrome that significantly impacts the quality of life of those affected, manifesting through intense joint pain and inflammation.", "TRASTORNOS MIELOPROLIFERATIVOS:Trastornos mieloproliferativos are disorders of the bone marrow that can result in increased production of ácido úrico due to high cell turnover."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}